      "observation": "UG03 improves matched-pair analysis, but final contexts still confuse lattice labels, metric populations and the evidence supporting equal-scale claims.",
      "evidence": "6pyy final synthesis labels 181.01933598375618->256 (j15->16) coarse although it is fine, and says one unbuilt R05/increase molecule may bias C. Remote records verify all50 coordinate rows contribute despite built49. 3w54 synthesis labels W2 256->128 as j16->15; actual index is14. It compares W1=256 against181.019 yet invokes equal-scale behavior. Its calibration p017 comparison also omits differing population size. All30 raw aggregates, four complete bound contexts and both retention ledgers were read.",
      "mechanism_applicability": "UniGuide condition maps and reverse differentiation separate endpoint residual, VJP and model/time prefactor. The flow guidance derivation is path-specific. We can interpret the frozen implementation and conditional paired interventions without changing it. C and build status have different definitions; the aggregation code includes all50 finite coordinate rows.",
      "skill_edit": "Require literal W1-W4/j mapping, explicit metric populations, matched-population qualification for calibration, and a fixed-state versus changed-trajectory explanation of scale effects. Verify actual equal scales before using that claim.",
      "expected_behavior": "UG04 reports consistent fine/coarse transitions and evidence-specific physical interpretation, and does not infer missing coordinates from failed chemistry or rank unmatched calibration as formal performance.",
      "next_version_falsifier": "Inspect all30 UG04 aggregates and its four bound contexts. Any decisive wrong j/mode/window claim, build-count C denominator claim, or equal-scale assertion with unequal cited S fails behavioral accuracy. Improved prose without improved frozen outcomes is not scientific success."
